#pragma once

// Real land/sea data for one specific location and radar radius, computed
// entirely offline using the companion desktop app's coastline pipeline
// (MicroRadarCompanion/CoastlineGenerator.cs) against real OSM data:
//  1. Coastline ways are reprojected into local meters, merged into a line
//     network, closed against a bounding box slightly larger than the actual
//     configured radar radius so every way forms a proper closed ring.
//  2. NetTopologySuite's Polygonizer reconstructs actual closed land/sea
//     polygons from that network.
//  3. Each polygon is classified land or sea by voting across many points
//     along its own real-coastline boundary edges (offset slightly into the
//     polygon's interior, and only counted if genuinely close to a real
//     segment) - not by testing a single interior/representative point,
//     which turned out to be unreliable for large, complex regions (a
//     whole harbour system, an isthmus): different points within the SAME
//     connected region can be nearest to entirely unrelated stretches of
//     coastline, giving contradictory answers for what should be one
//     consistent classification.
//  4. For each of the device's actual 60x60 render grid cells (matching
//     CoastlineManager::GRID_SIZE/CELL_PX and the Projection::ToScreen
//     formula exactly), the real-world land area fraction within that cell
//     is computed by exact polygon intersection, and the cell is only
//     recorded here if land covers the MAJORITY of it.
//
// This location (Auckland Airport, NZ) is a public landmark chosen
// specifically so this example data doesn't reveal anyone's real home
// location in this public repository - swap in your own coordinates and
// regenerate via the companion app for your own device.
//
// This is a plain point cloud on the wire: each entry is the center of one
// already-decided device grid cell. Rendering just projects each point onto
// the screen grid and marks that cell as land directly - no segment/nearest-
// neighbor geometry needed on the device, and since the array is flash-
// resident, no heap allocation either.
//
// Regenerate this file if the device is relocated OR the radar radius
// changes (the per-cell majority decision was computed for one specific
// radius - see EMBEDDED_COASTLINE_RADIUS_USED below).

